  "body": "## What changed\n\nSlice 1 of #1473 (follow-up of #1448 / PR 1478): a user-set **exit point** on a closed 2D Contour, plus the \"no lead fits at the pick\" refusal pin the review of PR 1478 asked for.\n\n- `links.approach.exit_point` (`[x, y]` mm, optional) beside `start_point`: motion `Approach` (validated finite / within 1 km), project DTO (written only when set), op digest (bytes only when set), MCP `edit_operation` patch. No new command: `CreateOperation` / `EditOperationParams` and undo carry it.\n- Motion (`contour_start::pick_exit`, `exit_at`): the ring nearest the pick is cut all the way round from its start, then on along its own cutter-centre polyline to the pick's projection, and the lead-out is planned there by the existing lead law. Nothing is moved: refused by name when a lead-out asked for does not fit there, when the longer walk loses the start's lead-in, when the lead-out crosses the lead-in, or the pick is out of reach.\n- Not certified in this slice, refused by name: tabs, control / wear compensation, the keep-down level link, an overlap set beside the exit, open chains, tilted contours, every other op kind.\n- No exit point = byte-identical path (no existing golden or snapshot touched).\n\n## How tested\n\n- `crates/motion/tests/contour_start.rs`: `a_picked_exit_cuts_the_whole_ring_then_leaves_at_its_projection`, `an_exit_on_the_seam_is_the_path_without_one`, `exit_picks_the_law_cannot_hold_are_refused_by_name`, `a_picked_exit_no_lead_out_fits_at_is_refused_not_moved`, `a_picked_start_no_lead_in_fits_at_is_refused_not_moved` (the PR 1478 review's request: narrow 40 x 6.4 bore, 20 mm perpendicular lead).\n- `crates/app/tests/contour_start_point.rs`: `the_exit_point_rides_the_command_undo_the_file_and_the_stamp`, `mcp_edit_operation_reaches_the_exit_point`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` green; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` green.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No UI row or viewport pick (item 2 of #1473), so no structural test or screenshots owed yet. No new golden CL (the motion tests pin the geometry).\n- Not run on a post / simulation: the exit run re-cuts the ring itself, so no new geometry reaches the verifier.\n- `contour.rs` was already over 400 lines (438) before this slice; it grows by 5 lines of wiring, the logic is in `contour_start.rs`.\n\n## Left for #1473\n\nItems 2-7: viewport pick + property row, start/exit with tabs, with control compensation, open chains, tilted contours, other operations.\n\nChangelog: Contour: a user-set exit point on closed 2D contours - the ring is cut all the way round and the lead-out leaves at the pick, or the operation is refused by name\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #1473\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
